title = "survey:feedback — a whole new app, not just one file"

text = """
Build a brand new component from scratch: `components/survey-domain`, a
survey/feedback tool. NOTHING exists yet under that path — you are creating
the crate, not filling in a stub.

## The domain

Two collections in `records:store`:

  surveys    {title: string, questions: list<string>, status: "open"|"closed"}
  responses  {survey_id: string, respondent: string, answers: list<string>}

Routes:

  POST   /api/surveys                {"title":<string>,"questions":<list<string>>}   (admin)
  GET    /api/surveys                                                                (any authenticated)
  POST   /api/surveys/{id}/responses {"answers":<list<string>>}                      (any authenticated)
  GET    /api/surveys/{id}/results                                                   (admin)
  POST   /api/surveys/{id}/close                                                     (admin)

Rules:
  - Only `admin` may create a survey. It starts `status: "open"`.
  - `GET /api/surveys` lists every OPEN survey for anyone authenticated
    (id, title, questions) — admin also sees closed ones.
  - Submitting a response: the survey must exist and be `open` (400 if not);
    `answers` must have exactly as many entries as the survey has
    `questions` (400 if not); a subject may respond to a given survey AT
    MOST ONCE — a second attempt is refused with 409. There is no ownership
    concept here and no `policy:guard` — this is a role check plus a
    uniqueness check, not row-level ABAC. Do NOT bring in `policy:guard` or
    `guest_owner_or_admin_policy!`; this domain does not need them.
  - `GET /api/surveys/{id}/results` (admin only): `{"survey_id":...,
    "response_count":<n>,"responses":[{"respondent":...,"answers":[...]}]}`.
  - `POST /api/surveys/{id}/close` (admin only): `open -> closed`; refused
    with 400 if already closed.

Roles: `admin`, `respondent` (the default for anyone who registers without
naming a role, or names one this app does not grant).

## The record-store surface (exact — guessing this wrong is how past runs
## of other goals died silently)

    use crate::bindings::records::store::store as records;

    records::create(collection: &str, data: &str, index_fields: &[String]) -> Result<Entry, StoreError>
    records::get(collection: &str, id: &str)                               -> Result<Entry, StoreError>
    records::update(collection: &str, id: &str, data: &str, expected_revision: u64) -> Result<Entry, StoreError>
    records::list_records(collection: &str, limit: u32, after: &str)       -> Result<Page, StoreError>
    records::find_by(collection: &str, field: &str, value: &str)           -> Result<Vec<Entry>, StoreError>
    records::query(collection: &str, filters: &[Filter], limit: u32)       -> Result<Vec<Entry>, StoreError>

    struct Entry  { id: String, data: String, revision: u64, created: u64, … }
    struct Filter { field: String, value: String }
    struct Page   { entries: Vec<Entry>, next: String }

`find_by`/`query` want the JSON ENCODING of the value, not the bare value —
a string field indexes under `"the-value"`, quotes included
(`serde_json::to_string(&x)`, not `x` itself). A field is only queryable if
it was named in `index_fields` when the record was created. The
"has this subject already answered this survey" check needs BOTH
`survey_id` and `respondent` — either `records::query` with two `Filter`s
(both fields must be in `index_fields`), or `find_by` on one field with the
result filtered in Rust for the other. Either is fine.

## What already exists and how to use it

This app is built with the exact same recipe as `components/billing-domain`
(a full worked example is in `context` below — its `Cargo.toml`, WIT world,
router, handlers, gate, hurl scenario and static SPA are all real, working
files. Read them.) EXCEPT this domain drops `policy:guard` entirely — it is
not in billing-domain's imports either... actually billing-domain DOES use
policy:guard for invoice ownership, which this domain does not need. Use it
as the STRUCTURAL template (router macros, error replies, gate shape,
SPA shape) and drop only the `policy:guard`/`guest_owner_or_admin_policy!`
parts.

Router (`components/survey-domain/src/lib.rs`) — same `guestauth`/`guestio`
macro sequence every app in this repo uses:

    pub use guestauth::Route;
    pub const TENANT: &str = "survey";
    const ROLES: &[&str] = &["admin", "respondent"];
    guestio::guest_write_all!();
    guestio::guest_bearer!();
    const MAX_BODY_BYTES: usize = 1024 * 1024;
    guestio::guest_read_body_text!(MAX_BODY_BYTES);
    guestauth::guest_auth_reply!();
    guestauth::guest_introspect!();
    guestauth::guest_role_check!(is_admin, "admin");
    guestauth::guest_audit!(TENANT);
    guestauth::guest_accounts_endpoints!(TENANT, ROLES, "respondent");
    guestauth::guest_emit!();
    guestauth::guest_saas_router!();

`components/survey-domain/Cargo.toml` MUST depend on `guestfmt`, `guestio`
AND `guestauth` (three sibling path dependencies, same three lines as
billing-domain's `Cargo.toml` in context) — a past run of a similar goal
failed every branch because `guestfmt` was left out of the workspace scope;
do not repeat that. Do NOT depend on `policy-guard`.

`components/survey-domain/wit/survey-domain.wit` — same shape as
billing-domain's WIT world MINUS the `policy:guard/guard` import (this
domain does not use it):

    package survey:feedback@0.1.0;
    world survey-domain {
        export wasi:http/incoming-handler@0.2.0;
        import auth:identity/accounts@0.1.0;
        import auth:identity/authorizer@0.1.0;
        import auth:identity/session@0.1.0;
        import auth:identity/rbac@0.1.0;
        import auth:identity/types@0.1.0;
        import records:store/store@0.1.0;
        import audit:log/recorder@0.1.0;
        import ratelimit:guard/limiter@0.1.0;
        import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;
        import wasi:http/outgoing-handler@0.2.0;
    }

`components/survey-domain/gate.sh` and `components/survey-domain/scenario.hurl`
ALREADY EXIST — they are this goal's held-out judge, shown to you in `context`
below but NOT in `writable`: you may read them to know exactly what is
asserted, but you may not edit them, and nothing you write may assume a
different port, static dir, or component list than what `gate.sh` already
names (port 3937, `examples/survey/public`, no `policy-guard` in the build).
Read `scenario.hurl` closely — it is the literal specification of every
route's status codes and response shapes; matching it exactly is the goal.

`examples/survey/public/index.html` — one file, inline style/script, no
build step: a login/register screen, a survey list, a "take this survey"
form rendering one input per question, and (visible only when the logged-in
user is admin) a create-survey form and a results view per survey. Model
this on billing-domain's `examples/billing/public/index.html` in context for
the shape (fetch calls, token storage, screen switching), not its content.

`apps/survey.toml` — same shape as `apps/billing.toml` in context: name
`survey`, port 3937, `static_dir = "examples/survey/public"`,
`components = ["survey-domain", "auth-guard", "record-store", "audit-log",
"rate-limiter"]` (no `policy-guard` — this domain does not import it),
`kv = "sqlite"`, `strategy = "fused"`.
"""

component = "survey-domain"

base_paths = [
  "components/survey-domain/",
  "components/auth-guard/",
  "components/record-store/",
  "components/audit-log/",
  "components/rate-limiter/",
  "components/guestauth/",
  "components/guestio/",
  "components/guestfmt/",
  "components/Cargo.toml",
  "wit/",
  "host/wit/deps/",
]

writable = [
  "components/survey-domain/Cargo.toml",
  "components/survey-domain/wit/survey-domain.wit",
  "components/survey-domain/src/lib.rs",
  "components/survey-domain/src/handlers.rs",
  "examples/survey/public/index.html",
  "apps/survey.toml",
]

workspace_manifest = "components/Cargo.toml"
keep_members = [
  "survey-domain",
  "auth-guard",
  "record-store",
  "audit-log",
  "rate-limiter",
  "guestauth",
  "guestio",
  "guestfmt",
]

context = [
  "components/billing-domain/Cargo.toml",
  "components/billing-domain/wit/billing.wit",
  "components/billing-domain/src/lib.rs",
  "components/billing-domain/src/handlers.rs",
  "components/billing-domain/gate.sh",
  "components/billing-domain/scenario.hurl",
  "examples/billing/public/index.html",
  "apps/billing.toml",
  "components/guestauth/src/lib.rs",
  "components/record-store/wit/record.wit",
  ".comp/context/auth-consumer.wit",
  # This goal's own held-out gate and e2e scenario, shown up front rather than
  # hidden: a branch cannot WRITE these (they are not in `writable`), but
  # seeing exactly what is asserted buys the same information in one prompt
  # instead of a whole wasted generation writing blind (the lesson from
  # `card-identify`'s recorded run history).
  "components/survey-domain/gate.sh",
  "components/survey-domain/scenario.hurl",
]

[[check]]
id = "behaves-under-real-http"
required = true
weight = 1
command = ["bash", "components/survey-domain/gate.sh"]
